# Normalize line endings on checkin so scripts that must run on Render's
# Linux container (start.sh in particular) can never accidentally get
# committed with CRLF endings by a contributor whose local git config
# (core.autocrlf) differs from this machine's. A CRLF shebang line fails on
# Linux with "/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory" — a
# deploy-breaking failure that's invisible in any local dev/test loop.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit belt-and-suspenders for anything invoked directly as a shell
# script, regardless of the general rule above.
*.sh text eol=lf
